<http://data.silknow.org/object/e28a7c2a-6657-3dd5-b704-129630f3170f>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "One of four pilaster panel tapestries commemorating the life of Pope Urban VIII.  This tapestry illustrates the facade of the church of Sta. Bibiana in Rome in a medallion, surmounted by a pediment bearing a cross, the papal tiara, keys, and shield with the Barberini arms.  Around the building are the words AEDE S BIBIANAE RESTITVTA ET ORNATA (\"The church of Saint Bibiana rebuilt and embellished.\")   Below the medallion is a pedestal with conventionalized foliated ornament and the Barberini bee woven with yellow The ground behind the pedestal is red. Above is a red swag with pendants of laurel leaves, a mask (woman) and a large yellow jar filled with flowers. Repairs and some slits."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/9fbfdfdc-73d4-34c1-9688-3899aa0187e5> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "One of four pilaster panel tapestries commemorating the life of Pope Urban VIII.  This tapestry illustrates the facade of the church of Sta. Bibiana in Rome in a medallion, surmounted by a pediment bearing a cross, the papal tiara, keys, and shield with the Barberini arms.  Around the building are the words AEDE S BIBIANAE RESTITVTA ET ORNATA (\"The church of Saint Bibiana rebuilt and embellished.\")   Below the medallion is a pedestal with conventionalized foliated ornament and the Barberini bee woven with yellow The ground behind the pedestal is red. Above is a red swag with pendants of laurel leaves, a mask (woman) and a large yellow jar filled with flowers. Repairs and some slits."@en ;
